    "title": "2026 Oscars Ceremony Kicks Off Soon - Los Angeles Today",
    "text": "Got story updates? Submit your updates here. ›The 2026 Oscars ceremony is set to take place at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles. Red carpet coverage will begin at 4 p.m. ET, with the official red carpet show starting at 6:30 p.m. ET. The Oscars ceremony itself will start at 7 p.m. ET/4 p.m. PT. Why it matters The Oscars are one of the most prestigious and widely watched awards shows in the entertainment industry, recognizing the best achievements in film over the past year. This year's ceremony is expected to draw significant attention, with two critically acclaimed films, 'Sinners' and 'One Battle After Another,' vying for top honors. The details The 2026 Oscars ceremony will be held at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles. Ryan Coogler's 'Sinners' leads the pack with a record-breaking 16 nominations, the most any single film has ever earned. It will be going head-to-head with Paul Thomas Anderson's 'One Battle After Another' in several of the night's biggest categories, including Best Picture. Red carpet coverage will begin at 4 p.m. ET on some networks.The official red carpet show will start at 6:30 p.m. ET.The Oscars ceremony itself will begin at 7 p.m. ET/4 p.m. PT. The players Ryan CooglerThe director of 'Sinners,' which has received a record-breaking 16 Oscar nominations.Paul Thomas AndersonThe director of 'One Battle After Another,' which is competing against 'Sinners' in several major categories. Got photos? Submit your photos here. › The takeaway This year's Oscars ceremony is shaping up to be a highly anticipated event, with two critically acclaimed films, 'Sinners' and 'One Battle After Another,' vying for the top prizes. The record-breaking number of nominations for 'Sinners' has added to the excitement and anticipation surrounding the ceremony.",
